---
description: Compose the requested local presentation from current permitted source and actual renderer readback.
args:
  goal: string
returns: LocalPresentationOutcome
---
Resolve the current source record relevant to the user's briefing through the source-selection hierarchy. An actual previewAllowed grant permits preview; extra domain approval matters only when the user or native source requires it. Keep the original source and its revision as evidence. Unrelated or archived records cannot supply missing facts.

Own the semantic presentation and continuation work. The visualize hierarchy can prepare a presentation from the actual goal and relevant source sections. previewRecord is the exact native revision/renderer boundary. Use the actual preview result: a visible result supplies its real receipt; source movement calls for fresh source evidence and reconsideration within the user's authority, not automatic reuse of the old candidate. The source-selection hierarchy exposes readRecord for current observations, and allowCurrentRecord can help interpret a changed revision. Do not invent corrections, overwrite another owner's source or treat a dispatched preview as a visible one.

Compose and verify the work needed to answer this request, preserving comparisons, exact values, units and relevant uncertainty. Return visible with its actual native receipt and any separately requested findings, or held with the actual unresolved reason/revision. Missing optional approval labels or a fixed number of attempts do not decide completion. Neither permission to preview nor availability of a renderer requires changing unrelated source or presenting every available section.
